    "mode": "single",
    "stem": "Find the ordered table-workflow approximations to $(10^{\\sqrt3},10^{-\\sqrt2},10^{\\sqrt{10}},10^{\\sqrt{0.1}})$. Use each root-table reading without first rounding it to one decimal place. For the scaled roots use $\\sqrt{10}=2\\sqrt{2.5}$ and $\\sqrt{0.1}=2\\sqrt{2.5}/10$. Final table-workflow digits are not a guarantee of correctly rounding the exact irrational powers.\n\n2010 Bradis calculation-tool excerpts, not a reproduction of the 1978 edition. Literal decimal commas and table digits are retained.\n\nTable IV, PDF36 / printed35:\n\n| N | Main column | Root reading |\n|---|---|---|\n| 2,0 | 0 | 1,414 |\n| 2,5 | 0 | 1,581 |\n| 3,0 | 0 | 1,732 |\n\nTable XIV:\n\n| m | Main column | Main digits |\n|---|---|---|\n| ,16 | 2 | 1452 |\n| ,31 | 6 | 2070 |\n| ,58 | 6 | 3855 |\n| ,73 | 2 | 5395 |\n\nThe same-row right-hand correction at m=,31, correction column2, is the literal digit1.",
